1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,640
The Rebrand I Wish I Could Redo.

2
00:00:03,216 --> 00:00:07,641
Last year, I worked on a rebranding
project for a small coffee company.

3
00:00:07,641 --> 00:00:12,635
Looking back, I wish I had listened to my
instincts from the beginning. If I had

4
00:00:12,635 --> 00:00:17,313
asked more questions in the first
meeting, I would have understood what the

5
00:00:17,313 --> 00:00:22,180
client really wanted. Instead, I opened
Illustrator and designed a logo in two

6
00:00:22,180 --> 00:00:22,496
days.

7
00:00:22,942 --> 00:00:26,542
When I presented it, the client looked
confused.

8
00:00:26,916 --> 00:00:29,076
"It's beautiful,".

9
00:00:29,531 --> 00:00:30,731
she said,

10
00:00:31,128 --> 00:00:32,968
"but it doesn't feel like us.".

11
00:00:33,352 --> 00:00:35,752
"What do you mean?" I asked.

12
00:00:36,176 --> 00:00:40,815
"If you had visited our shop, you would
have seen that we are warm and

13
00:00:40,815 --> 00:00:44,176
old-fashioned. This design looks cold and
modern.".

14
00:00:44,669 --> 00:00:49,936
I felt terrible. If only I had spent one
afternoon in her shop, I would have saved

15
00:00:49,936 --> 00:00:54,814
us all a lot of time. Without a proper
brief, I had worked completely in the

16
00:00:54,814 --> 00:00:59,626
dark. I had even chosen the colors
without checking her brand guidelines. I

17
00:00:59,626 --> 00:01:04,243
should have asked for them first,
otherwise the colors would never match

18
00:01:04,243 --> 00:01:06,909
her packaging, and of course they didn't.

19
00:01:07,294 --> 00:01:10,494
That evening, I called my colleague
Deniz.

20
00:01:10,876 --> 00:01:13,996
"I wish I hadn't rushed," I told him.

21
00:01:14,536 --> 00:01:16,456
"Don't be so hard on yourself,".

22
00:01:16,864 --> 00:01:17,664
he said.

23
00:01:18,095 --> 00:01:18,175
"

24
00:01:18,699 --> 00:01:22,860
But you should have shown her some
sketches first. If you had shared early

25
00:01:22,860 --> 00:01:27,020
ideas, she could have corrected you
before you spent two days on the final

26
00:01:27,020 --> 00:01:27,419
file.".

27
00:01:27,845 --> 00:01:31,685
"I know. I wish I had been more
patient.".

28
00:01:32,211 --> 00:01:36,371
"Well, it's not too late. Let's fix it
together.".

29
00:01:36,890 --> 00:01:41,719
We worked all weekend. But for Deniz, I
would have missed the new deadline. He

30
00:01:41,719 --> 00:01:46,861
reorganized my layers, and he reminded me
to export every file in the right format.

31
00:01:46,861 --> 00:01:51,752
If he hadn't done that, the developer
wouldn't have been able to use my assets,

32
00:01:51,752 --> 00:01:54,010
and we would have lost another week.

33
00:01:54,500 --> 00:02:00,005
In the end, the client loved the new
version. She even said it was better than

34
00:02:00,005 --> 00:02:05,366
she had imagined. Still, I can't stop
thinking about the first mistake. If I

35
00:02:05,366 --> 00:02:11,014
had taken the time to listen, I wouldn't
have wasted so much energy. Now, before

36
00:02:11,014 --> 00:02:16,805
every project, I ask for a clear brief, I
look at the brand guidelines, and I show

37
00:02:16,805 --> 00:02:21,380
early sketches. Otherwise, I know I will
repeat the same mistake.

